// spec: a wide string literal passed to a `const wchar_t (&)[N]` parameter in a constant evaluation, `len(L"ab")` (Unreal's `consteval TCheckedFormatStringPrivate(const TCHAR (&Fmt)[N])`): the array, N 3 (`3`)
// found by thread UE (2026-11-21): the literal's value came typed `const wchar_t[]`, no length, and the reference did not bind where wchar_t is 16 bits (Windows; Linux's 32-bit one bound); constBindParameter takes an array of no length whose elements are as many as the reference's array's as that array
template<int N> constexpr int len(const wchar_t (&s)[N]) { (void)s; return N; }

int main()
{
  constexpr int n = len(L"ab");
  std::println(n);
  return 0;
}
